    "organizingIdeaDescription": "The science of collecting, analyzing, visualizing, and interpreting data can inform understanding and decision making.",
    "guidingQuestion": "How can statistics support generalizations?",
    "learningOutcome": "Students interpret sample data.",
    "type": "Knowledge",
    "text": "A population is a complete set of elements, such as people, animals, objects, or events, that are the focus of a statistical question.",
    "sourcePage": 14,
    "source": "Alberta Draft Mathematics (7–9) Curriculum, June 2026, ©2026 Government of Alberta | Education and Childcare; Draft Curriculum: Optional Classroom Piloting in 2026–27"
