    "learningOutcome": "Students define solutions to single-variable linear inequalities.",
    "type": "Knowledge",
    "text": "An inequality can be solved by applying the same operations to expressions on both sides of the inequality, according to the properties of inequalities, including\n• if a < b, then a + c < b + c for any real numbers a, b, and c (addition property)\n• if a < b, then ac < bc for any real numbers a, b, and c, where c > 0 (multiplication property)\n• if a < b, then ad > bd for any real numbers a, b, and d, where d < 0 (multiplication property)",
    "sourcePage": 6,
    "source": "Alberta Draft Mathematics (7–9) Curriculum, June 2026, ©2026 Government of Alberta | Education and Childcare; Draft Curriculum: Optional Classroom Piloting in 2026–27"
